# Folder structure

## Max 4 files at the root of any folder

Count only files directly in the folder (not inside subfolders). When a 5th file is needed, move related files into a subfolder.

Typical root contents:
- `index.ts` — barrel exports (required when the folder is imported from outside)
- One orchestrator (e.g. `HomePage.tsx`, `StoreLayout.tsx`) when it exists
- At most 1–2 other top-level files before splitting

## Subfolders by domain, not by file type

Prefer grouping by feature/domain:

| Area | Example subfolders |
|------|-------------------|
| `components/home` | `banner/`, `sections/` |
| `components/shop` | `catalog/`, `product/`, `reviews/modals/`, `reviews/forms/` |
| `components/layout` | `store/`, `dashboard/`, `info/` |
| `components/admin/catalog` | `detail/`, `shared/` |
| `lib` | `auth/`, `catalog/`, `products/`, `seo/`, `drive/` |

## Barrel exports (`index.ts`)

Every module folder exposed to the rest of the app must have an `index.ts` that re-exports its public API.

```typescript
// ✅ Import from barrel
import { ProductDetail, ShopFilters } from "@/components/shop";
import { fetchGroupedProductsPage } from "@/lib/catalog";

// ❌ Avoid deep paths when a barrel exists
import { ProductDetail } from "@/components/shop/product/ProductDetail";
```

## When reorganizing

1. Create subfolders and move files (preserve git history with `git mv`).
2. Add or update `index.ts`.
3. Fix internal relative imports inside the folder.
4. Update external imports to use the barrel path.
